    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for coredns",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for coredns fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in coredns:\n\n- Update to 1.15.0:\n  * Fixes VUL-0: CVE-2026-78669: excessive CPU consumption in HTTP/2 (boo#1285501)\n    and CVE-2026-97032: HTTP/2 server crash due to HPACK encoder\n    race (boo#1287577) by bumping vendored golang.org/x/net to\n    v0.60.0.\n  * Drops temporary google.golang.org/grpc pin for CVE-2026-84304 as upstream\n    now vendors v1.84.0.\n  * plugin/cache: cache SERVFAIL when resolver fails without response\n  * plugin/forward: support DNS-over-QUIC upstreams\n  * core: add opt-in JSON logging with structured DNS query fields\n  * New features: SIIT support, expr-lang templates, PROXY protocol v2 metadata\n  * Bumped minimum go build requirement to 1.26.0\n  * Skip flaky timing/network-sensitive tests in %check (TestHealthMaxFails,\n    TestReconnect, TestRace, TestSecondaryZoneNotify, TestPeriodicWeightUpdate)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-packagehub-702",
        "title": "Patchnames"
